## Verdict

The implementation is **essentially complete against intent.** Pass 1 shows a
faithful preliminary→spec translation (one minor optionality firming on the
lowest-priority C.2 item, plus fidelity corrections that only tightened the
pointers). Pass 2 shows every spec commitment (A–D) shipped across 13
gate-green, code-judge-approved committed slices, with no dropped requirement and
no product-scope creep. The three residuals are all documented, low-risk, and do
not block the spec's stated acceptance criteria (which are unit- and
headless-verified): two are end-to-end verification boundaries left thin because
no shipping data exercises them (C.1's view-only μ path — no magnetic built-in
exists; D.2/D.3's engine group-suppression — carried by pre-existing wiring), and
one is a genuine feature narrowing (C.2 auto-wrap-on-drag, deferred to a future
layout pass). The highest-priority follow-up, if any is taken, is the C.2 wrap —
it is the only place a user-visible behaviour the spec named is only partially
delivered.
